WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.837
<i>♪ It seems today that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.838 --> 00:08.174
<i>♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:08.175 --> 00:11.969
<i>♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.970 --> 00:14.847
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.848 --> 00:18.200
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.201 --> 00:21.606
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.607 --> 00:23.189
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.190 --> 00:25.024
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:25.025 --> 00:30.155
<i>♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:37.287 --> 00:42.544
<i>♪ In a one-horse open sleigh ♪</i>

00:44.211 --> 00:48.212
Aw, this is one of those weird
third-verse-nobody-knows songs.

00:48.213 --> 00:50.317
<i>♪ Winter killed our child ♪</i>

00:50.318 --> 00:52.093
<i>♪ Medicine was rare ♪</i>

00:52.094 --> 00:54.220
<i>♪ He ran outside in his bare feet ♪</i>

00:54.221 --> 00:56.469
<i>♪ And then he died right there ♪</i>

00:56.470 --> 00:59.055
Glad that's over. Oh, God, there's four.

00:59.056 --> 01:00.851
<i>♪ Please don't free the slaves ♪</i>

01:00.852 --> 01:03.104
<i>♪ It's a bad idea ♪</i>

01:03.105 --> 01:05.273
<i>♪ They'll try to get back at us ♪</i>

01:05.274 --> 01:07.693
<i>♪ And that'si our biggest fear, oh... ♪</i>

01:10.362 --> 01:12.363
And now, Adam West High School Choir's

01:12.364 --> 01:15.393
original Christmas song, "Die Hard."

01:15.394 --> 01:16.532
I see those looks.

01:16.533 --> 01:19.036
Yes, the movie was
originally released in summer,

01:19.037 --> 01:21.622
but it took place on Christmas Eve,

01:21.623 --> 01:23.289
which makes it a Christmas film.

01:23.290 --> 01:26.419
I guess we don't need this for anything.

01:27.879 --> 01:31.716
<i>♪ Die Hard ♪</i>

01:31.717 --> 01:35.428
<i>♪ Die Hard ♪</i>

01:35.429 --> 01:39.033
<i>♪ John McClane ♪</i>

01:39.034 --> 01:42.393
<i>♪ And his wife ♪</i>

01:42.394 --> 01:48.393
<i>♪ Yippee-ky-yay, (BLEEP) ♪</i>

01:49.901 --> 01:55.892
<i>♪ Yippee-ky-yay, (BLEEP) ♪</i>

02:02.203 --> 02:03.998
Chris and Meg alert.

02:03.999 --> 02:06.834
Oh. We have to go, uh,
call our congressman.

02:06.835 --> 02:08.919
- What are they...?
- Hey, Mr. Quagmire.

02:08.920 --> 02:11.368
Getting ready for the birth of Christ?

02:11.369 --> 02:13.120
Which happened!

02:13.121 --> 02:14.685
Chris. Megan.

02:14.686 --> 02:16.761
- Gross.
- So, how did you like the show?

02:16.762 --> 02:18.179
I-I didn't love it.

02:18.180 --> 02:19.972
H-Hey, have you guys seen that mom

02:19.973 --> 02:21.474
who wears a swimsuit for a bra?

02:21.475 --> 02:22.850
She can't come to these.

02:22.851 --> 02:25.811
Her ex-husband has a
restraining order against her.

02:25.812 --> 02:27.802
Boy, her stock just keeps going up.

02:27.803 --> 02:29.025
So, Christmas, huh?

02:29.026 --> 02:31.942
- You guys must be excited.
- Ugh, not at all.

02:31.943 --> 02:33.750
It's always disappointing.

02:33.751 --> 02:35.988
Just a reminder
of how truly lonely I am.

02:35.989 --> 02:39.075
- Hey-hey! Seamus, my man!
- Oh, hello.

02:39.076 --> 02:41.240
Allow me to introduce you
to my son, Woody.

02:41.241 --> 02:42.495
- Hey, Woody.
- Hey.

02:42.496 --> 02:44.538
He's gonna be a new character
on the show.

02:44.539 --> 02:46.457
You're barely a character on the show.

02:46.458 --> 02:47.834
More than Woody!

02:51.922 --> 02:53.881
Meg, there's a lot I have
to get done here,

02:53.882 --> 02:56.509
so I need you to take Stewie
to the mall to meet Santa.

02:56.510 --> 02:58.177
- Okay. Sure.
- Great.

02:58.178 --> 03:01.306
Now, why don't you go warm up
the car for your little brother?

03:02.808 --> 03:04.809
She's gone. Quick!

03:04.810 --> 03:06.770
Let's take the picture
for the Christmas card.

03:12.359 --> 03:15.403
I sent the wrong picture to Walgreens.

03:21.284 --> 03:22.993
Oh, look, there's all the Jewish kids

03:22.994 --> 03:24.495
sitting on the rabbi's lap,

03:24.496 --> 03:26.789
<i>where he asks them for something.</i>

03:26.790 --> 03:30.000
I want a new TV,
and it can't be a Vizio.

03:30.001 --> 03:32.002
Sony or Samsung only.

03:32.003 --> 03:35.181
And I need it all set up
before I turn it on.

03:35.182 --> 03:38.676
I don't want to have to do
any of the things!

03:38.677 --> 03:40.387
Okay, little guy. You're up.

03:50.689 --> 03:54.403
So, little boy, what would you
like for Christmas?

04:02.868 --> 04:04.702
What's wrong, little boy?

04:04.703 --> 04:06.745
Don't be scared of Santa.

04:06.746 --> 04:08.289
Come on, Stewie. It's okay.

04:08.290 --> 04:10.207
Just sit on Santa's lap.

04:10.208 --> 04:13.667
Ugh. Some people push their kids
to do stuff way too soon.

04:13.668 --> 04:15.629
Do you agree, Doctor Baby-Violin?

04:15.630 --> 04:16.922
I really do.

04:19.950 --> 04:22.094
Is it okay if I just hold
him for the picture?

04:22.095 --> 04:24.638
Ho, ho, ho. Of course.

04:24.639 --> 04:26.224
Sit right here, young lady.

04:27.601 --> 04:31.061
Here you go, Stewie.
Santa's no one to be scared of.

04:31.062 --> 04:34.815
He's kind and warm.
He loves unconditionally,

04:34.816 --> 04:37.443
and... and he makes...

04:37.444 --> 04:40.654
everyone feel so... so...

04:40.655 --> 04:42.156
Meg, what are you doing?

04:42.157 --> 04:44.867
You look like Mom when she sits
on the washing machine.

04:44.868 --> 04:47.953
Now, what would you like
for Christmas, little boy?

04:47.954 --> 04:49.955
Shut up, everyone! Shut up! Shut up!

04:49.956 --> 04:51.332
Just shut up!

04:51.333 --> 04:55.503
<i>♪ O come, let us adore him ♪</i>

04:55.504 --> 05:00.257
<i>♪ O come, let us adore him ♪</i>

05:00.258 --> 05:05.262
<i>♪ O come, let us adore him... ♪</i>

05:05.263 --> 05:08.016
What, uh... Wh-What just happened?

05:09.142 --> 05:11.393
I'll have what she's having.

05:11.394 --> 05:14.522
Okay. She had six
well-done hamburger patties

05:14.523 --> 05:16.524
jammed into a hard taco shell.

05:16.525 --> 05:18.859
Oh. I just want to feel like that.

05:18.860 --> 05:22.196
Okay. I mean, I can get it
for you, but it's a weird order.

05:22.197 --> 05:24.032
The chef was not happy about it.

05:45.677 --> 05:47.973
Are you ready for me, Meg?

06:02.487 --> 06:04.822
- Are you ready to get up?
- Huh?

06:04.823 --> 06:06.950
I said it's time to get up.

06:08.034 --> 06:09.326
It's 2:00.

06:09.327 --> 06:11.537
I've never seen you sleep so soundly.

06:11.538 --> 06:13.038
What's going on?

06:13.039 --> 06:14.665
Mom, I think I met someone.

06:14.666 --> 06:16.500
Oh, Meg, that's amazing.

06:16.501 --> 06:18.085
I want to know all about him.

06:18.086 --> 06:19.420
What's his name?

06:19.421 --> 06:21.714
Let's just call him "Beard Boy."

06:21.715 --> 06:25.717
<i>Oh! It's like I'm in Sex with the City.</i>

06:25.718 --> 06:28.762
It all happened so quick,
but I really feel something.

06:28.763 --> 06:32.182
- Am I crazy?
- No. Trust your instincts.

06:32.183 --> 06:33.681
You've got to chase this feeling.

06:33.682 --> 06:35.480
Go find Beard Boy.

06:35.481 --> 06:37.981
I will, Mom. I will!

06:39.274 --> 06:41.108
What was going on in here?

06:41.109 --> 06:42.693
The windows are steamed up

06:42.694 --> 06:44.821
like when Subway's making the bread.

06:45.905 --> 06:47.698
Hey. What's going on in here?

06:47.699 --> 06:49.450
We're making the bread, sir.

06:49.451 --> 06:51.869
Good. Now get back to making sandwiches

06:51.870 --> 06:54.038
with the shiniest turkey on earth!

06:54.039 --> 06:55.706
<i>Subway. Have it your way.</i>

06:55.707 --> 06:57.705
<i>If your way is very wet.</i>

07:05.746 --> 07:07.645
Can you pass the milk?

07:07.646 --> 07:09.845
Stewie? Can you pass the milk?

07:09.846 --> 07:13.369
<i>- ♪ O come, all ye faithful... ♪
- Shut up, everyone!</i>

07:13.370 --> 07:15.506
<i>Shut up! Shut up!</i>

07:15.507 --> 07:16.976
<i>Just shut up!</i>

07:16.977 --> 07:18.729
Hey. Pass the milk.

07:18.730 --> 07:20.064
What the hell's going on with you?

07:20.065 --> 07:22.066
I-I haven't slept in two days.

07:22.067 --> 07:24.151
Is this still that Santa thing?
Get over it.

07:24.152 --> 07:26.487
You didn't see the things I saw.

07:26.488 --> 07:28.322
<i>♪ O come ♪</i>

07:28.323 --> 07:32.159
<i>♪ All ye faithful... ♪</i>

07:32.160 --> 07:34.912
I mean, Santa Claus
was bouncing us on his knee.

07:34.913 --> 07:36.330
And it got a little faster,

07:36.331 --> 07:38.332
then faster, and the more he bounced,

07:38.333 --> 07:39.954
the bigger Meg's eyes got.

07:39.955 --> 07:42.712
It was... it was...
Just look at the picture!

07:45.048 --> 07:46.590
Wow. Okay.

07:46.591 --> 07:48.842
Uh, Stewie,
I think I know what happened.

07:48.843 --> 07:51.345
I can't tell you explicitly,
since we're owned by Disney,

07:51.346 --> 07:53.430
but let me just say that

07:53.431 --> 07:56.141
Santa made her "Little Mermaid" "Moana."

07:56.142 --> 07:58.769
- Oh.
- Exactly.

07:58.770 --> 08:02.232
Brian, would you hand me
the Fat Man's fancy puking hat?

08:13.493 --> 08:14.951
God, this hat is deep.

08:14.952 --> 08:18.623
Now, there's my hat.
Kids, I'm off to the opera.

08:19.901 --> 08:22.210
This opera stinks.

08:26.214 --> 08:27.840
It was awful, Rupert.

08:27.841 --> 08:30.342
And worst of all,
I didn't even get to ask Santa

08:30.343 --> 08:31.825
for the Vitamix.

08:31.826 --> 08:34.805
Blender? It's more than a blender.

08:34.806 --> 08:37.224
Stewie. I'm gonna
take you back to the mall

08:37.225 --> 08:38.642
to sit on Santa's lap.

08:38.643 --> 08:40.103
Oh, my God, I've got to hide!

08:43.606 --> 08:46.695
How did she find me?
That's my best hiding spot. No!

08:46.696 --> 08:49.229
Oh, and by the way, Rupert,
after what I saw,

08:49.230 --> 08:52.697
I know you've been faking it
this whole time.

09:03.920 --> 09:05.669
Meg, please don't.

09:05.670 --> 09:08.718
Listen, I've got seven dollars
in my piggy bank.

09:08.719 --> 09:11.364
It's yours. No?
All right, uh, I'll kill Chris.

09:11.365 --> 09:12.637
You want me to kill Chris?

09:12.638 --> 09:14.678
Who do you want me to kill? Chris? No?

09:14.679 --> 09:15.846
Okay. I got it.

09:15.847 --> 09:18.265
Next road show, Stewie and Meg. Promise.

09:18.266 --> 09:21.560
<i>♪ We're off on the road to Ohio. ♪</i>

09:21.561 --> 09:23.854
High in the middle
and round at both ends!

09:23.855 --> 09:25.439
Meg, I love our road show.

09:25.440 --> 09:27.066
- Next.
- No!

09:28.902 --> 09:31.278
Huh. Something's different.

09:31.279 --> 09:34.176
Hey, uh, Meg? Uh, can you cut that out?

09:34.177 --> 09:35.290
Dad?!

09:35.292 --> 09:36.909
Please don't tell your
mother about this.

09:36.910 --> 09:38.577
I took an extra job.

09:38.578 --> 09:41.538
I don't make much money,
and Christmas is very expensive.

09:41.539 --> 09:45.000
Dad? I'm gonna ask you one question,

09:45.001 --> 09:48.378
and how you answer it will
determine the rest of my life.

09:48.379 --> 09:51.423
Were you the Santa
at this mall yesterday?

09:51.424 --> 09:53.217
- No.
- Oh, thank God.

09:53.218 --> 09:55.427
Now, Meg, I got a question for you:

09:55.428 --> 09:57.763
Is there really a weight limit
for the escalator,

09:57.764 --> 09:59.473
or did I just meet some mean kids?

09:59.474 --> 10:01.391
Hey, Peter, let's keep it moving.

10:01.392 --> 10:03.393
Some stockbrokers are gonna
throw me into a gong later.

10:03.394 --> 10:06.480
Excuse me. Do you remember
the Santa from yesterday?

10:06.481 --> 10:08.649
Lady, I've been thrown
head first into so many gongs,

10:08.650 --> 10:10.400
I don't remember my own name.

10:10.401 --> 10:13.077
I think he was just a temp.
I'd try the Warwick Mall.

10:13.078 --> 10:14.901
Thanks. Stewie, come on.

10:14.902 --> 10:16.582
We're going to the Warwick Mall.

10:16.583 --> 10:18.077
Stewie?

10:20.744 --> 10:22.580
Chocolate sample.

10:24.438 --> 10:26.274
Again.

10:28.490 --> 10:31.089
Just leave the carton.

10:31.090 --> 10:33.169
- Santa's the best.
- I'm gonna ask for a bike.

10:33.170 --> 10:35.592
I'm also enthusiastic about Santa.

10:35.593 --> 10:38.512
All hail the great Santa Claus.

10:38.513 --> 10:41.472
Yeah. This guy gets it.

10:41.473 --> 10:44.092
Wait a minute.
That noise seems negative.

10:44.093 --> 10:46.854
Santa's a good guy
'cause he keeps a list?

10:46.855 --> 10:48.948
You know who else kept a list? Hitler.

10:48.949 --> 10:51.483
My uncle who moved
to the Idaho wilderness

10:51.484 --> 10:52.778
says Hitler was a great man.

10:52.779 --> 10:54.788
There you are. Come on.

10:54.789 --> 10:57.197
We've got to visit Santa
at another mall.

10:57.198 --> 10:59.406
I can't go back to Santa, man! I can't!

10:59.407 --> 11:01.826
- Hello again.
- Hi.

11:01.828 --> 11:05.082
That's the guy that was peeing
in the women's bathroom.

11:11.045 --> 11:15.132
Stewie, when this is over,
I'm buying you a new toy.

11:15.133 --> 11:17.509
Meg, when this is over,
I'm putting rocks in my pockets

11:17.510 --> 11:19.909
and walking into the mall fountain.

11:19.910 --> 11:21.847
How much longer is this gonna take?

11:21.848 --> 11:23.807
I don't know. 400 minutes?

11:23.808 --> 11:25.851
One reason I work as a seasonal elf

11:25.852 --> 11:27.519
is I'm not great at time estimates.

11:27.520 --> 11:29.813
- Next.
- See? 400 minutes.

11:29.814 --> 11:33.398
Even a broken clock
is right six times a day.

11:33.399 --> 11:35.442
He's very scared,
so I have to sit here with him.

11:35.443 --> 11:36.961
Would you mind bouncing me a little?

11:36.962 --> 11:39.230
Um, okay. I guess I can do that.

11:40.243 --> 11:42.743
Hey, come on, a little harder than that.

11:42.744 --> 11:45.372
- Look, I don't feel comf...
- Please! It's Christmas. Please!

11:45.373 --> 11:46.890
What does... what does
that have to do with...

11:46.892 --> 11:48.740
Just do it!

11:49.376 --> 11:51.919
<i>♪ The itsy-bitsy spider ♪</i>

11:51.920 --> 11:54.171
<i>♪ Went up the water spout... ♪</i>

11:54.172 --> 11:56.006
Wait, wait, th-this isn't working.

11:56.007 --> 11:58.082
Were you at the Quahog Mall last night?

11:58.083 --> 12:01.845
No. L-Last night, I was weeping
outside my ex-wife's apartment.

12:01.846 --> 12:03.719
I drank too much
and went over to yell at her.

12:03.720 --> 12:05.179
Yeah, he's not your guy, Meg.

12:05.180 --> 12:08.018
They said my Santa would
be here, and you're not him.

12:08.019 --> 12:09.970
I'm sorry. Story of my life.

12:09.971 --> 12:12.105
I live to disappoint women, apparently.

12:12.106 --> 12:15.071
Well, where is he? Where's my Santa?

12:15.072 --> 12:17.306
- I don't know!
- I need to find him.

12:17.307 --> 12:19.169
He made me a woman!

12:19.170 --> 12:20.865
Where is he?

12:23.451 --> 12:24.725
He's a phony!

12:24.726 --> 12:26.937
A great, big phony!

12:26.938 --> 12:29.706
Excuse me, ma'am, I'm gonna
give you just 600 minutes

12:29.707 --> 12:31.415
- to get out of here.
- But you don't understand.

12:31.416 --> 12:33.758
One, two, 600 minutes.

12:33.759 --> 12:35.945
That's it. Security!

12:35.946 --> 12:37.699
What took you so long?

12:37.700 --> 12:38.965
Let me go.

12:38.966 --> 12:42.135
Lady, by the power vested in me
by Paul Blart,

12:42.136 --> 12:44.096
you are now banned from this mall

12:44.097 --> 12:45.961
and every mall in this county.

12:45.962 --> 12:50.060
W-Wait. I need my little brother.

12:50.061 --> 12:51.771
Stewie!

12:54.565 --> 12:57.527
Time to sleep in heavenly peace.

13:00.723 --> 13:03.391
Wow, looks like that baby is all wet.

13:05.747 --> 13:07.494
Classic Woody.

13:07.495 --> 13:09.205
This is Woody.

13:14.919 --> 13:17.838
So, you want to tell me
why you were assaulting Santa

13:17.839 --> 13:19.423
in front of the whole mall?

13:19.424 --> 13:21.216
What about Beard Boy?

13:21.217 --> 13:23.510
Santa is Beard Boy.

13:23.511 --> 13:25.470
You're in love with Santa?

13:25.471 --> 13:26.847
Maybe.

13:26.848 --> 13:29.641
He gave me my first... you know.

13:29.642 --> 13:32.394
He just bounced me on his lap,
and the next thing you know,

13:32.395 --> 13:34.187
- I saw Jimmy Connors.
- You saw Jimmy Connors.

13:34.188 --> 13:36.690
It happens to every girl
their first time.

13:36.691 --> 13:38.358
You'll never see him again, by the way.

13:38.359 --> 13:40.152
I won't? Why not?

13:40.153 --> 13:43.113
I don't know.
That's God's trick on women.

13:43.114 --> 13:45.365
It's your first time,
followed by a lifetime

13:45.366 --> 13:46.784
of diminishing returns.

13:52.705 --> 13:55.793
I wonder what I'll see on my first time.

14:13.601 --> 14:16.518
I can't let Stewie grow up
scared of Santa Claus.

14:18.316 --> 14:20.150
Ho, ho, ho.

14:20.151 --> 14:22.022
Santa? Is that really you?

14:22.023 --> 14:24.237
- Sure is.
- Well, how'd you get in?

14:24.238 --> 14:26.406
- Through the window.
- It was just unlocked?

14:26.407 --> 14:29.101
Like, anybody can just come
through my window at any time?

14:29.102 --> 14:31.079
- I really don't like...
- Forget about that.

14:32.371 --> 14:34.414
I know you're having a tough time.

14:34.415 --> 14:37.417
I just wanted to tell you
that everything is fine.

14:37.418 --> 14:40.921
Meg is entering probably
the most horny part of her life.

14:40.922 --> 14:43.006
This could just as easily have happened

14:43.007 --> 14:44.800
while she was riding a horse
or something.

14:44.801 --> 14:46.551
I'm just sorry you had to see it.

14:46.552 --> 14:49.721
Okay. Don't want people
just coming in whenever.

14:49.722 --> 14:53.183
Stewie, that Christmas magic
you think you lost,

14:53.184 --> 14:55.102
it can't just disappear.

14:55.103 --> 14:57.896
I'm still the same guy
you've always loved.

14:57.897 --> 15:00.814
Thanks, Santa. I feel better.

15:00.815 --> 15:03.110
Just try to have a good Christmas.

15:03.111 --> 15:05.237
Uh, speaking of that, I want a new dog.

15:05.238 --> 15:07.114
What's wrong with the dog you have?

15:07.115 --> 15:10.033
Eh, he's okay.
I just... I just want a new one.

15:10.034 --> 15:12.661
Maybe you can spend more time
with the old one

15:12.662 --> 15:15.330
- before you make any decisions.
- Nah. Want a new one.

15:15.331 --> 15:17.457
Thanks, Santa.
Can you leave from the door?

15:17.458 --> 15:19.004
I'm kind of freaking
over the window thing.

15:19.005 --> 15:20.586
Sure.

15:22.547 --> 15:24.297
Oh, my God. Santa?

15:24.298 --> 15:26.970
- I want a new dog.
- Oh, come on!

15:31.347 --> 15:32.848
There you are.

15:32.849 --> 15:34.891
I had a hell of a time
finding your room.

15:34.892 --> 15:36.603
Can I come in?

15:36.604 --> 15:38.904
- Cigarette?
- No.

15:38.905 --> 15:40.494
Mind if I have one?

15:43.151 --> 15:46.653
So, you want to talk about
this whole Santa's lap thing?

15:46.654 --> 15:50.490
Dad, this stuff, I-I think it's
gonna be hard for you to hear.

15:50.491 --> 15:52.200
Oh, don't worry, Meg.
I brought this handkerchief

15:52.201 --> 15:55.000
